  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}+2)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x}\u226b\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}+2)=\\infty .\n$$",
